WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.120
Film Courage: Would you rather give your past&nbsp;
self advice or ask your future self a question?

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:13.520
Logan Burdick, Screenwriter: That's a&nbsp;
deep one. Ask my future self a question?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:22.880
I guess that I only get to do one,&nbsp;
those are both really positive things.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:34.480
I’m going to go with ask my future self&nbsp;
a question just because I feel luckily&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:44.320
I have the a personality in which I'm always&nbsp;
trying to figure things out and come up with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:52.320
new and novel approaches to any problem either&nbsp;
creatively or from a career perspective. I would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.320 --> 00:01:01.360
to imagine that only gets better with age. I would&nbsp;
hope that future me would have a lot of insight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:09.520
now because I guess the other problem with&nbsp;
that scenario is do you listen to you anyway&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:17.600
right? Because that's I feel again at least&nbsp;
myself and a lot of people I think that you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:25.840
are a lot more headstrong when you haven't had as&nbsp;
much experience and you haven't failed in whatever&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:34.000
crazy ways that you failed. You think everything&nbsp;
that you're going to do is the correct answer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:42.160
and so I think that it's a little hard to shake&nbsp;
yourself out of that until you've actually had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:49.760
that experience. You go Oh that really did&nbsp;
not work but yeah I imagine that young me&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:55.120
probably would have been a little hubristic&nbsp;
and would not necessarily take old me's advice.

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:58.960
Film Courage: What would be the question&nbsp;
that you would ask your future self?

00:01:59.480 --> 00:02:02.960
Logan: The question I would ask my future self?

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:07.840
Film Courage: Yeah, Dear Logan, I have a question…

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:13.840
Logan: A thousand percent legitimately I would ask&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:27.440
what steps do I need to take now to ensure&nbsp;
that I'm holistically happiest in the future?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:37.600
I think a thing that a lot of entertainment&nbsp;
people struggle with or again maybe not a lot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:44.080
of it or maybe it's just me but I think that&nbsp;
at least for me personally it's the idea of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:52.480
again of chasing something that makes you&nbsp;
feel fulfilled. It's very easy to be okay&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:58.800
I've never had a movie made. Okay I had a movie&nbsp;
made but it wasn't a big enough movie, how do I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:03.280
get a bigger movie made? Okay but it didn't star&nbsp;
these [people]. It's very easy to get into that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:13.120
mindset and I think that it's really important&nbsp;
even though it's hard to try to take a step back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:23.680
and go okay but but life still keeps going on&nbsp;
you need to try to focus on what makes you happy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:30.320
in this moment what makes you feel fulfilled&nbsp;
in this moment and not get too caught up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:38.480
in in the in the chasing of goals I do&nbsp;
obviously goals are extremely important&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:51.120
you're never going to reach whatever you're&nbsp;
never going to reach the fulfillment that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:56.240
you want if you're not setting goals for yourself&nbsp;
and you're not taking these steps to actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.240 --> 00:04:01.920
achieve things but I think that it's very&nbsp;
easy to make that solely the focus and when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:06.320
that's solely the focus there's a lot that&nbsp;
you're missing that's going on all around you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:14.480
we were talking about originally this idea of&nbsp;
okay does it look exactly again what I thought&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:22.160
of when I was a child my life yes or no is one&nbsp;
question but is what it is still really great&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:32.080
if you're looking to poke holes in something&nbsp;
you can always poke holes I'm sure that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:40.160
the richest most successful people on planet&nbsp;
earth have all the same problems that like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:50.400
everyone has and the same the same regrets and the&nbsp;
same lack of whatever they feel they're missing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:55.840
it's important to try to not focus on that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.040 --> 00:05:04.240
so bring it back around I think that that's what&nbsp;
I would be most interested in what strategies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:12.800
future me has come up with to again to effectively&nbsp;
live in the moment and not get caught up in all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.800 --> 00:05:19.120
the what-ifs I think it's great that you're&nbsp;
talking about chasing this these goals because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:24.560
I think that's so easy to do whether it's an&nbsp;
indie film or if you on a higher budgeted film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.560 --> 00:05:29.360
because there's a lot of hoopla when a trailer&nbsp;
comes out and then you're reading comments and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:34.320
hopefully they're positive and then if the film&nbsp;
screen somewhere okay but some of that stuff is so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:40.960
short-lived and then it's on to the next project&nbsp;
for so many people either whether they're working&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:46.480
on it or whether they're going to see it and so&nbsp;
a lot of that is just this it's the evolution&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:53.920
of a movie it's a a circle and and some of&nbsp;
that what seems satisfying is so short-lived&nbsp;&nbsp;

